      "sections":[{"client_key":"recovery_negatives_recover_section","title":"Not non lavora da solo","instructions":"Scegli l'ausiliare prima di costruire la negativa.","selection_mode":"fixed","feedback_timing":"question_end","questions":[
        {"client_key":"recovery_neg_recover_teaching","type":"content_block","title":"Negatives: trova l'ausiliare","prompt":"Prima di esercitarti","instructions":"Confronta be, Present Simple, Past Simple e i tempi con un ausiliare già presente.","instruction_language":"it","level":"A2","topic":"negatives","subtopic":"core_system","primary_skill":"grammar","learning_objective":"Build standard negative forms by choosing the correct auxiliary and main-verb form.","difficulty":"support","content":{"educational_schema_version":1,"template_id":"educational-content-block-v1","variant":"grammar","body":"In inglese la negativa normalmente usa un ausiliare. Con be aggiungi not direttamente a be. Con i verbi normali al Present Simple usi don't/doesn't; al Past Simple usi didn't. Dopo don't/doesn't/didn't il verbo resta base.","intro":"La domanda non è soltanto dove mettere not, ma quale ausiliare appartiene alla struttura.","sections":[
          {"key":"be","type":"pattern","title":"Be + not","body":"Con am/is/are/was/were non aggiungere do.","pattern":"subject + be + not + ...","examples":[{"text":"She isn't tired.","highlight":["isn't"]},{"text":"They weren't at school.","highlight":["weren't"]}]},
          {"key":"present","type":"pattern","title":"Present Simple: don't/doesn't + base","body":"I/you/we/they → don't; he/she/it → doesn't. Il verbo principale torna base.","pattern":"subject + don't/doesn't + base verb","examples":[{"text":"I don't work on Sundays.","highlight":["don't work"]},{"text":"He doesn't like coffee.","highlight":["doesn't like"]}]},
          {"key":"past","type":"pattern","title":"Past Simple: didn't + base","body":"Didn't porta già il passato, quindi il verbo principale non resta al Past Simple.","pattern":"subject + didn't + base verb","examples":[{"text":"We didn't go out.","highlight":["didn't go"]},{"text":"Sara didn't call me.","highlight":["didn't call"]}]},
          {"key":"continuous","type":"rule","title":"Se c'è già be, aggiungi not lì","body":"Nei tempi continui, not segue am/is/are o was/were.","examples":[{"text":"I'm not studying now.","highlight":["'m not studying"]},{"text":"They weren't waiting.","highlight":["weren't waiting"]}]},
          {"key":"perfect","type":"rule","title":"Present Perfect: have/has + not","body":"Anche qui l'ausiliare è già presente.","examples":[{"text":"She hasn't finished yet.","highlight":["hasn't finished"]}]},
          {"key":"mistake","type":"mistake","title":"Non marcare due volte persona o passato","body":"Doesn't/didn't portano già l'informazione grammaticale.","correct":{"text":"He doesn't work here. · They didn't go.","highlight":["doesn't work","didn't go"]},"incorrect":{"text":"He doesn't works here. · They didn't went.","highlight":["works","went"]}},
          {"key":"recap","type":"recap","title":"Procedura","points":["Il verbo è be? → be + not.","Verbo normale al presente? → don't/doesn't + base.","Verbo normale al passato? → didn't + base.","C'è già un ausiliare nel tempo? → metti not dopo quell'ausiliare.","Non lasciare not da solo davanti al verbo principale."]}
        ]},"grading":{"mode":"automatic","weight":0,"nearly_correct_multiplier":0.5},"feedback":{},"diagnostics":{"tested_codes":[],"fallback_error_code":null},"tags":["recovery","negatives","recover","structured-teaching"],"foundation_links":[]},
